course: dictionary
lesson: 9891
title: A bird that came back from the dead
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you may never have seen, so you work out what they mean from the clues around them. «Animals thought extinct that turn up alive again are called Lazarus species.» Extinct means no longer alive anywhere, so a Lazarus species is a kind of animal that was lost and then found alive again.
explain: The takahe is a large bird from New Zealand. The clue is in its description: flightless means it cannot fly. Blue-green feathers, a big red beak and red legs help you picture it, even if you have never seen one.
explain: Takahe comes from the Māori language, which is spoken in New Zealand. Many words from other languages are new to us, so the sentences around them and a dictionary can help.
fact: Takahe is a noun: it names a thing, here a large bird.
fact: «Takahe» means a large, flightless bird from New Zealand, with blue-green feathers, a big red beak and red legs.
fact: Flightless means it cannot fly.
fact: «Extinct» means no longer alive anywhere in the world.
fact: The takahe was thought to be extinct, but it was found again in 1948 and is now protected.
exercise: «The takahe is a large, flightless bird from New Zealand.» What does flightless mean? | It can fly very high | It has no feathers | It lives in the sea | *It cannot fly
exercise: What colour are the feathers of the takahe? | *Blue-green | Black and white | Golden | Red
exercise: «Animals thought extinct that turn up alive again are called Lazarus species.» What does extinct mean? | *No longer alive anywhere | Found in New Zealand | Very large | Brightly coloured
test: Which parts of the takahe are red? | Its back and head | Its feathers and eyes | *Its beak and legs | Its wings and tail
test: Why was the takahe famous in 1948? | It was declared extinct for the first time | *It was found alive again after being thought extinct | It laid its first egg in a zoo | It flew across the sea to New Zealand
exam: Which word in «Animals thought extinct that turn up alive again are called Lazarus species» means no longer alive anywhere? | Species | Lazarus | *Extinct | Animals
